# Coding Standards

## TypeScript Guidelines
- Strict TypeScript configuration
- Use interfaces for data structures  
- Proper nullability for optional fields
- zod validation for runtime data validation
- Avoid `any` type

## Components Structure
- One component per file
- Descriptive naming: `PatientOverview.tsx`, `FacilityList.tsx`
- Organize by feature: Patient/, Facility/, etc.
- WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility compliance
- Proper error boundaries

## UI Standards
- shadcn/ui for standard components
- CAREUI for custom components
- Tailwind CSS design system
- Mobile-first responsive design

## Data Management
- TanStack Query for API data
- React Context for app state
- Proper error handling
- Data validation patterns

## File Naming
- kebab-case directories: `patient-management/`
- PascalCase components: `PatientList.tsx`
- Camel case hooks: `useData.ts`

## Testing
- Cypress E2E for critical workflows
- Accessibility testing
- Follow patterns in `cypress/docs/`
- Write clear test descriptions
